{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41272","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72878","text":"Round 27, pass B1.2.1 — "},{"id":"spn-72879","marks":["code"],"text":"emit()"},{"id":"spn-72880","text":" was a hidden semantic relation"}]},{"id":"blk-41273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72881","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your find, reproduced, plus its dual and three more of the same species. No behaviour changed."}]},{"id":"blk-41274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72882","text":"Gate: grid "},{"id":"spn-72883","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.37.0"},{"id":"spn-72884","text":" (80 entries / 374 citations) · "},{"id":"spn-72885","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72886","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72887","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.5.0"},{"id":"spn-72888","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-72889","marks":["bold"],"text":"241/241"},{"id":"spn-72890","text":" · lowering "},{"id":"spn-72891","marks":["bold"],"text":"13/13"},{"id":"spn-72892","text":" film-evidenced · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · bridge 48/48 · film 16/16 · twelve paired probes · harness 9/9 · runner 3/3 · pack 24/24, 0 skipped · NUL sweep 0. "},{"id":"spn-72893","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-72894","text":" byte-identical — "},{"id":"spn-72895","marks":["bold"],"text":"thirty-first"},{"id":"spn-72896","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41275","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72897","text":"1. Your finding, reproduced"}]},{"id":"blk-41276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72898","text":"Mutate "},{"id":"spn-72899","marks":["code"],"text":"TARGET_ENCODING.add"},{"id":"spn-72900","text":" and nothing else:"}]},{"id":"blk-41277","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"LOWERING_SEM_ID                    MOVED      lsem-d95ee1cb… → lsem-39ec194a…\nINSTANTIATION_SEM_ID               UNCHANGED  isem-bf9434fc…\nTARGET_TEMPLATE_ENCODING_SEM_ID    UNCHANGED  tenc-2adf4d28…\ntarget_template_sem_id             UNCHANGED  tmpl-ebab76bb…\nemitted term bytes                 CHANGED"},{"id":"blk-41278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72901","text":"Your base "},{"id":"spn-72902","marks":["code"],"text":"lsem-d95ee1cb…"},{"id":"spn-72903","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72904","marks":["code"],"text":"isem-bf9434fc…"},{"id":"spn-72905","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-72906","marks":["code"],"text":"tmpl-ebab76bb…"},{"id":"spn-72907","text":" are exactly the values I get. Our mutated "},{"id":"spn-72908","marks":["code"],"text":"lsem"},{"id":"spn-72909","text":" differ ("},{"id":"spn-72910","marks":["code"],"text":"39ec194a…"},{"id":"spn-72911","text":" vs your "},{"id":"spn-72912","marks":["code"],"text":"6e445936…"},{"id":"spn-72913","text":") because we perturbed the same field with different text — which is the right reason for them to differ, and why the finding is the "},{"id":"spn-72914","marks":["bold"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-72915","text":" and not the hex."}]},{"id":"blk-41279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72916","marks":["bold"],"text":"Confirmed:"},{"id":"spn-72917","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72918","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_SEMANTICS"},{"id":"spn-72919","text":" named its "},{"id":"spn-72920","marks":["bold"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-72921","text":" by id and its "},{"id":"spn-72922","marks":["bold"],"text":"codomain"},{"id":"spn-72923","text":" in prose, "},{"id":"spn-72924","marks":["code"],"text":"\"TRVM-TERM-CANON-v1 / ic32 executable text, via emit()\""},{"id":"spn-72925","text":". The whole executable encoding reached the relation's identity as eight characters inside an English sentence."}]},{"id":"blk-41280","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72926","text":"2. The dual, which your patch would have left in place — please rule on this"}]},{"id":"blk-41281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72927","text":"Your prescribed fix adds "},{"id":"spn-72928","marks":["code"],"text":"TARGET_EXECUTABLE_ENCODING_SEM_ID"},{"id":"spn-72929","text":" to instantiation. It does "},{"id":"spn-72930","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-72931","text":" remove "},{"id":"spn-72932","marks":["code"],"text":"target_encoding: TARGET_ENCODING"},{"id":"spn-72933","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-72934","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_SEMANTICS"},{"id":"spn-72935","text":". Under that fix an emitter change moves "},{"id":"spn-72936","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-72937","text":" ids. I removed it, and I think it is the same defect facing the other way:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72938","text":"Before B1.2, "},{"id":"spn-72939","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-72940","text":" produced ic32 text and the executable encoding genuinely "},{"id":"spn-72941","marks":["bold"],"text":"was"},{"id":"spn-72942","text":" lowering's codomain. B1.2 moved the codomain onto the template, fixed the "},{"id":"spn-72943","marks":["code"],"text":"LoweringReceipt"},{"id":"spn-72944","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72945","marks":["bold"],"text":"one declaration below"},{"id":"spn-72946","text":", and left this line pointing two layers downstream."}]}],"id":"blk-41282","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72947","text":"That is the identical class as the receipt still ending at "},{"id":"spn-72948","marks":["code"],"text":"target_term_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-72949","text":" — the one B1.2 caught. Consequence: an emitter change "},{"id":"spn-72950","marks":["bold"],"text":"re-identified every `LoweringReceipt` ever issued"},{"id":"spn-72951","text":", for a relation lowering does not perform."}]},{"id":"blk-41285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72952","marks":["bold"],"text":"The rule I wrote into the law, and the thing to rule on:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72953","text":"A relation's identity must commit, "},{"id":"spn-72954","marks":["bold"],"text":"by content and not by name"},{"id":"spn-72955","text":", to exactly the encodings of its own "},{"id":"spn-72956","marks":["bold"],"text":"domain and codomain — no more and no fewer."}]}],"id":"blk-41286","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72957","marks":["bold"],"text":"MEASURED, three directions"},{"id":"spn-72958","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-72959","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering_check"},{"id":"spn-72960","text":" case "},{"id":"spn-72961","marks":["code"],"text":"emit-is-not-a-hidden-relation"},{"id":"spn-72962","text":"):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41290","spans":[{"id":"spn-72963","text":"mutation"}]},{"id":"blk-41291","spans":[{"id":"spn-72964","marks":["code"],"text":"lsem"}]},{"id":"blk-41292","spans":[{"id":"spn-72965","marks":["code"],"text":"isem"}]},{"id":"blk-41293","spans":[{"id":"spn-72966","marks":["code"],"text":"tenc"}]}],"id":"blk-41289","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41294","spans":[{"id":"spn-72967","marks":["code"],"text":"TARGET_ENCODING.add"},{"id":"spn-72968","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-72969","marks":["code"],"text":".dup_label_policy"},{"id":"spn-72970","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-72971","marks":["code"],"text":".numbers"}]},{"id":"blk-41295","spans":[{"id":"spn-72972","text":"same"}]},{"id":"blk-41296","spans":[{"id":"spn-72973","marks":["bold"],"text":"MOVED"}]},{"id":"blk-41297","spans":[{"id":"spn-72974","text":"same"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41298","spans":[{"id":"spn-72975","marks":["code"],"text":"op_lowering_rules.const"},{"id":"spn-72976","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-72977","marks":["code"],"text":".add"}]},{"id":"blk-41299","spans":[{"id":"spn-72978","marks":["bold"],"text":"MOVED"}]},{"id":"blk-41300","spans":[{"id":"spn-72979","text":"same"}]},{"id":"blk-41301","spans":[{"id":"spn-72980","text":"same"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41302","spans":[{"id":"spn-72981","marks":["code"],"text":"TARGET_TEMPLATE_ENCODING.grammar"},{"id":"spn-72982","text":" (shared boundary)"}]},{"id":"blk-41303","spans":[{"id":"spn-72983","marks":["bold"],"text":"MOVED"}]},{"id":"blk-41304","spans":[{"id":"spn-72984","marks":["bold"],"text":"MOVED"}]},{"id":"blk-41305","spans":[{"id":"spn-72985","marks":["bold"],"text":"MOVED"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41306","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72986","text":"3. Removing it exposed that the lowering map was never written down"}]},{"id":"blk-41307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72987","marks":["code"],"text":"lowered_ops"},{"id":"spn-72988","text":" says "},{"id":"spn-72989","marks":["italic"],"text":"which"},{"id":"spn-72990","text":" ops lower; the template encoding says what the codomain's nodes "},{"id":"spn-72991","marks":["italic"],"text":"are"},{"id":"spn-72992","text":". "},{"id":"spn-72993","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nothing said a `const` becomes a `church` node"},{"id":"spn-72994","text":", or that "},{"id":"spn-72995","marks":["code"],"text":"add"},{"id":"spn-72996","text":" preserves operand order. You made me freeze the "},{"id":"spn-72997","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-72998","text":" rule at B1.1; "},{"id":"spn-72999","marks":["code"],"text":"const"},{"id":"spn-73000","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73001","marks":["code"],"text":"add"},{"id":"spn-73002","text":" were left implicit, so "},{"id":"spn-73003","marks":["code"],"text":"const(n) → church(n+1)"},{"id":"spn-73004","text":" would have contradicted no sentence in the hashed semantics. New "},{"id":"spn-73005","marks":["code"],"text":"op_lowering_rules"},{"id":"spn-73006","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73007","marks":["italic"],"text":"An identity that cannot move when its map changes is the same defect as one that moves when its map has not."}]},{"id":"blk-41309","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73008","text":"4. The two refusal vocabularies were crossed"}]},{"id":"blk-41310","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73009","marks":["code"],"text":"TARGET_ENCODING.refusals"},{"id":"spn-73010","text":" held four "},{"id":"spn-73011","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-*"},{"id":"spn-73012","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73013","marks":["bold"],"text":"source-fragment"},{"id":"spn-73014","text":" refusals that cannot arise while"}]}],"id":"blk-41311","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73015","text":"emitting. Once those bytes carry an identity, renaming "},{"id":"spn-73016","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-negative"},{"id":"spn-73017","text":" moves the "},{"id":"spn-73018","marks":["italic"],"text":"executable encoding's"},{"id":"spn-73019","text":" id without touching the encoding."}]},{"id":"blk-41314","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73020","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_SEMANTICS.refusal_semantics"},{"id":"spn-73021","text":" held "},{"id":"spn-73022","marks":["code"],"text":"emit-unbound-port"},{"id":"spn-73023","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73024","marks":["code"],"text":"template-malformed"},{"id":"spn-73025","text":", **neither"}]}],"id":"blk-41315","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73026","text":"reachable from "},{"id":"spn-73027","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-73028","text":"** — it emits only zero-port templates it built itself."}]},{"id":"blk-41318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73029","text":"Swapped. The witness now "},{"id":"spn-73030","marks":["bold"],"text":"drives every name lowering claims"},{"id":"spn-73031","text":" to an actual refusal."}]},{"id":"blk-41319","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73032","text":"5. Emission ruled INTO instantiation, with your trigger written down"}]},{"id":"blk-41320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73033","text":"I took your smaller fix on the split question, and recorded your larger point "},{"id":"spn-73034","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the hashed record"},{"id":"spn-73035","text":" rather than in a comment, so the boundary stays a decision:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73036","text":"A third relation with its own "},{"id":"spn-73037","marks":["code"],"text":"emission_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73038","text":" is the more faithful decomposition — a correct port substitution can coexist with an incorrect emitter — and it is "},{"id":"spn-73039","marks":["bold"],"text":"not taken while `emit()` is neither independently reused nor independently theorem-bearing. When either becomes true, split it"},{"id":"spn-73040","text":", and this relation's codomain becomes the closed TEMPLATE rather than the executable term."}]}],"id":"blk-41321","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41323","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73041","text":"6. Your two stale diagnostics, and two more I found"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41325","spans":[{"id":"spn-73042","text":"#"}]},{"id":"blk-41326","spans":[{"id":"spn-73043","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41327","spans":[{"id":"spn-73044","text":"status"}]}],"id":"blk-41324","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41328","spans":[{"id":"spn-73045","text":"1"}]},{"id":"blk-41329","spans":[{"id":"spn-73046","text":"receipt prose says "},{"id":"spn-73047","marks":["code"],"text":"target_term_sem_id"}]},{"id":"blk-41330","spans":[{"id":"spn-73048","marks":["bold"],"text":"DERIVED"},{"id":"spn-73049","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-73050","marks":["code"],"text":"Object.keys(receipt)"},{"id":"spn-73051","text":", not repaired"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41331","spans":[{"id":"spn-73052","text":"2"}]},{"id":"blk-41332","spans":[{"id":"spn-73053","text":"\"six identities\" is obsolete"}]},{"id":"blk-41333","spans":[{"id":"spn-73054","marks":["bold"],"text":"the count is gone"},{"id":"spn-73055","text":", see below"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41334","spans":[{"id":"spn-73056","text":"3"}]},{"id":"blk-41335","spans":[{"id":"spn-73057","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERED_OPS"},{"id":"spn-73058","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-73059","marks":["code"],"text":"IMPLEMENTED_LOWERED_OPS"},{"id":"spn-73060","text":" + the stale comment"}]},{"id":"blk-41336","spans":[{"id":"spn-73061","text":"done"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41337","spans":[{"id":"spn-73062","text":"4"}]},{"id":"blk-41338","spans":[{"id":"spn-73063","marks":["bold"],"text":"`law:derivation.canonical-lowering@1` described the pre-B1.2 world"}]},{"id":"blk-41339","spans":[{"id":"spn-73064","text":"mine — see below"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41340","spans":[{"id":"spn-73065","text":"5"}]},{"id":"blk-41341","spans":[{"id":"spn-73066","marks":["bold"],"text":"`artifact_versions` had 3 entries no check read"}]},{"id":"blk-41342","spans":[{"id":"spn-73067","text":"mine — see below"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73068","marks":["bold"],"text":"On (2), I did not fix the count — I removed it."},{"id":"spn-73069","text":" You said don't get obsessed with the number, cover every node the refinement claims to distinguish. "},{"id":"spn-73070","marks":["code"],"text":"REFINEMENT_CHAIN"},{"id":"spn-73071","text":" is now machine-readable with an "},{"id":"spn-73072","marks":["code"],"text":"exercised"},{"id":"spn-73073","text":" flag and a "},{"id":"spn-73074","marks":["code"],"text":"why_not"},{"id":"spn-73075","text":" per unexercised node. The case "},{"id":"spn-73076","marks":["bold"],"text":"derives"},{"id":"spn-73077","text":" its set, "},{"id":"spn-73078","marks":["bold"],"text":"fails"},{"id":"spn-73079","text":" if a declared node is not wired into the witness, and "},{"id":"spn-73080","marks":["bold"],"text":"names"},{"id":"spn-73081","text":" the unexercised ones ("},{"id":"spn-73082","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiation_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73083","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73084","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73085","text":"). The headline derives too. There is no count to get wrong. "},{"id":"spn-73086","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering-refinement@1"},{"id":"spn-73087","text":" had the same six enumerated in the "},{"id":"spn-73088","marks":["bold"],"text":"law"},{"id":"spn-73089","text":", so the registry and the witness were stale together — which is how a hand-typed count survives a reading."}]},{"id":"blk-41344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73090","marks":["bold"],"text":"(4) is the worse one, and grid_check was holding it in place."},{"id":"spn-73091","text":" The statement printed the receipt as "},{"id":"spn-73092","marks":["code"],"text":"{program_sem_id, lowering_sem_id, target_term_sem_id}"},{"id":"spn-73093","text":" and called parameterized-versus-instantiated "},{"id":"spn-73094","marks":["bold"],"text":"DEFERRED"},{"id":"spn-73095","text":" — three passes after B1 decided it and B1.1 ruled the framing a false choice. The assertion defending it read "},{"id":"spn-73096","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"must keep the inputs model DEFERRED AND NAMED\""},{"id":"spn-73097","text":". "},{"id":"spn-73098","marks":["bold"],"text":"A check that requires a stale record to stay stale is a ratchet, not an instrument."},{"id":"spn-73099","text":" Also: the lookup carried no revision filter and its sibling loop pinned "},{"id":"spn-73100","marks":["code"],"text":"revision === 1"},{"id":"spn-73101","text":", so every assertion below them read whichever entry sat earliest in the array. Three laws revised to "},{"id":"spn-73102","marks":["code"],"text":"@2"},{"id":"spn-73103","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-73104","marks":["code"],"text":"@2"},{"id":"spn-73105","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-73106","marks":["code"],"text":"@3"},{"id":"spn-73107","text":"; all three predecessors kept as non-canonical history, "},{"id":"spn-73108","marks":["code"],"text":"defect_class: record-staleness"},{"id":"spn-73109","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73110","marks":["code"],"text":"accepted_false_verdict: false"},{"id":"spn-73111","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73112","marks":["bold"],"text":"(5) I found by tripping over my own half-applied bump."},{"id":"spn-73113","text":" grid_check's "},{"id":"spn-73114","marks":["code"],"text":"declared"},{"id":"spn-73115","text":" list named three files; "},{"id":"spn-73116","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact_versions"},{"id":"spn-73117","text":" carried six. Half the map was a hand-maintained number with "},{"id":"spn-73118","marks":["bold"],"text":"no instrument behind it"},{"id":"spn-73119","text":" — it had carried "},{"id":"spn-73120","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73121","text":" through 0.2.0, 0.3.0 and 0.4.0 unverified. I bumped to 0.5.0, grid_check said "},{"id":"spn-73122","marks":["bold"],"text":"PASS"},{"id":"spn-73123","text":" with the grid still declaring 0.4.0, and the same edit had moved the file "},{"id":"spn-73124","marks":["italic"],"text":"header"},{"id":"spn-73125","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-73126","marks":["code"],"text":"v0.5.0"},{"id":"spn-73127","text":" while leaving "},{"id":"spn-73128","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_VERSION"},{"id":"spn-73129","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-73130","marks":["code"],"text":"\"0.4.0\""},{"id":"spn-73131","text":" — the identical defect inside one file. All six entries are now read and the map must be "},{"id":"spn-73132","marks":["bold"],"text":"fully covered"},{"id":"spn-73133","text":" by its reader."}]},{"id":"blk-41346","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73134","text":"7. Nothing behavioural changed, and it is checkable"}]},{"id":"blk-41347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73135","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiate()"},{"id":"spn-73136","text":" still throws · "},{"id":"spn-73137","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-73138","text":" still refuses as "},{"id":"spn-73139","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-input-not-implemented"},{"id":"spn-73140","text":" · the three port falsifiers are still "},{"id":"spn-73141","marks":["code"],"text":"DECLARED"},{"id":"spn-73142","text":" and unwritten. "},{"id":"spn-73143","marks":["code"],"text":"add(2,3)"},{"id":"spn-73144","text":" still reaches the "},{"id":"spn-73145","marks":["bold"],"text":"same 129 characters"},{"id":"spn-73146","text":", the same six-frame film, the same normal form, the same 5. Both relation ids moved — "},{"id":"spn-73147","marks":["code"],"text":"lsem-84c93447…"},{"id":"spn-73148","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73149","marks":["code"],"text":"isem-6ac0ea7b…"},{"id":"spn-73150","text":" — and that is the point: "},{"id":"spn-73151","marks":["bold"],"text":"both relations' commitments changed and neither relation's behaviour did."}]},{"id":"blk-41348","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73152","text":"8. One debt NAMED rather than paid — and it makes your B2 item 6 mandatory"}]},{"id":"blk-41349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73153","text":"Once emission belongs to instantiation, "},{"id":"spn-73154","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-73155","text":" calling "},{"id":"spn-73156","marks":["code"],"text":"emit()"},{"id":"spn-73157","text":" means "},{"id":"spn-73158","marks":["bold"],"text":"lowering performs part of instantiation"},{"id":"spn-73159","text":" — and the entire 13-case refinement witness runs off "},{"id":"spn-73160","marks":["code"],"text":"low.target_term"},{"id":"spn-73161","text":", so it reaches native execution "},{"id":"spn-73162","marks":["bold"],"text":"without passing through the relation this round just made load-bearing"},{"id":"spn-73163","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73164","text":"Nothing identity-bearing flows from it (the receipt ends at the template; the term's id is the kernel's). Recorded as "},{"id":"spn-73165","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_STATUS.emission_debt"},{"id":"spn-73166","text":" with a named closer. Your regression theorem — "},{"id":"spn-73167","marks":["code"],"text":"add(2,3)"},{"id":"spn-73168","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-73169","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiate({})"},{"id":"spn-73170","text":" reaching the same bytes — is therefore "},{"id":"spn-73171","marks":["bold"],"text":"mandatory, not tidy"},{"id":"spn-73172